<article> <header class="hero"> <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"> <a href="/">Home</a> <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="9 18 15 12 9 6"/></svg> <a href="/glossary">Glossary</a> <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="9 18 15 12 9 6"/></svg> <span>CBPR+</span> </nav> <div class="hero-badge"><span class="pulse-dot"></span><span style="position:relative;z-index:1">Glossary · Schemes & Rules</span></div> <h1><span class="accent">CBPR+</span></h1> <p class="page-meta">Glossary entry · Last reviewed 26 July 2026</p> <!-- ANSWER BLOCK — picked up by speakable schema --> <p class="answer-block"><strong>CBPR+ (Cross-Border Payments and Reporting Plus)</strong> is the SWIFT usage guideline that defines how ISO 20022 messages are populated for cross-border payments on the SWIFT network. It evolves through annual November Standards Releases; <strong>SR 2026 (15 November 2026)</strong> removes the fully unstructured postal address from the accepted profile for newly initiated payments.</p> </header> <section class="section"> <div class="section-label">In Practice</div> <h2 class="section-title">How CBPR+ works in practice</h2> <div class="content-block"><p>CBPR+ has been "Aligned" since November 2025: fully structured and hybrid formats are enabled and validation enforces the CPMI harmonisation requirements — technical annex hybrid profile across pacs.008, pacs.009, pacs.004 and camt messages. Rejection of non-compliant addresses happens at the point of entry into the network.</p></div> <p class="src">Source: BIS PIE taskforce, Fostering ISO 20022 harmonisation §3.1.2 / p12-6; the ioNova Postal Address Specification v2.0 §10.7 (Table 25) and glossary ("SR 2026"); Swift, Removal of unstructured address.3 / p1-1.</p> <div class="content-block"><p>Parent reference: <a href="/address-intelligence/structured-address-mandate">ISO 20022 structured address mandate</a>.</p></div> </section> <section class="section"> <div class="section-label">Citations</div> <h2 class="section-title">Sources</h2> <div class="sources-list"> <h3 class="sources-subhead">Standards &amp; regulatory sources</h3>
